gin{aligned}r((2+5\\text{i})t) & ={e}^{(2+5\\text{i})t} \\\\ {\\alpha }_{1}(2+5\\text{i})t+{\\alpha }_{0} & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\ (2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0})+5{\\alpha }_{1}\\text{i}t & ={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)+\\text{i}\\,{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we equate the real and imaginary parts, and solve for ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t) \\\\ 5t{\\alpha }_{1} &={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,⇒\\,\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}{\\alpha }_{1} &=\\frac{1}{5t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ {\\alpha }_{0} &={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t))\\end{aligned}\\right.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${\\alpha }_{1}$ and ${\\alpha }_{0}$ into the expressions for the required entries of ${e}^{At},$ we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3{\\alpha }_{1}t+{\\alpha }_{0} & =-3\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t+{e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\frac{2}{5}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{5}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\frac{2}{5}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)) \\\\ 5{\\alpha }_{1}t & =5\\cdot \\frac{1}{5t}{e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\cdot t \\\\  & ={e}^{2t}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{e}^{At}={e}^{2t}\\begin{bmatrix}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & -2\\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t) & \\operatorname{sin}⁡(5t)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5t)\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186308673 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186307693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308673 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186308240 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186308673 #edb/ref 1069 "q-3347